    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "W.5 Grant, Jr. President\nBaron Long Managing Director\nU.S.GRANT HOTEL\nEUROPEAN PLAN\nSAN DIEGO, CAL.\nарч. 14.1927\nDear Mr. Biply:\nIt is diffient to obtair\nmuch information here regarding\ncommercial seablanes. al do not\nunderstand to whom her. he hider\nrefered when he told you that\na number of types were being\nmanafactured on the west coact.\n3 he Danglao Co has comfleta\na few for the havy; also th\nBacing Corh. Ryan hurlines has\nnot, a yet agent any hea\ntheir planes with pontoons,",
      "U.S Grant, Jr., President\n2\nBaron Long Managing Director\nU.S.GRANT HOTEL\nEUROGEAN FLAN\nSAN DIEGO, CAL.\nthee arganizations are the andy\nproduction manufacturers of\naircraft west of the mountaris.\nI understand that pontoons\nhave proven satiefactary ou\nthe tahiskored Sravelain and\nFakher tyhe planes, and that\nwhen larger shif are used more\nhover is required as in the\nLowing flying boat\nEda duralumin pontoons\nwholesale at $1200 and Hamiltons\nstal at $2,000.",
      "U.S Grant, Jr. President\n3\nBaron Long. Managing Director\nU.S.GRANT HOTEL\nEUROPEAN FLAN\nSAN DIEGO, CAL.\nEither of there makes would\nstand fairly rough usage but na\nseaplane can strike lange driftwood\nat high feed without being\ndamaged.\nwast of the seaplane manefoctuas\nare located in the east and I\nwill get mare data in hew york.\nI have been delayed here\ndue to the late arrival of our\nenquie and also waiting for\nthe final streambining to\nbe comfleted. I am curtainly",
      "U.S Grant. Jr., President\nBaron Long,Managing Director\nU.S. GRANT HOTEL\nEUROPEAN PLAN\nSAN DIEGO, CAL.\nsorry not to have been able\nto arrive in St. Lanis an afare\nbut the fortary is working\novertime on the plane and e\nstill hape to be in hew york\non tho 28h\nDue to the fresent uncertain\nsituation l suggest that na\nplans be mode which will require\nmuch time at St. foris.\nI will wire you the trime\nof arried as soon as possible.\nSincerely,\nCharles Q. Kindlingh"
    ],
